 "standard_text": "Mental mathematics: number bonds to 20; addition and subtraction facts to 20; doubling and halving; use the relationship between addition and subtraction.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 2 maths worksheets: number bonds, addition and subtraction facts to 20, doubles, halves and fact families. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Make 10 first.",
 "key_sub": "Start a fact family from the total.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Know the bonds to 10: 7 + 3, 6 + 4 …</li><li>Use them for 20: 17 + 3 = 20.</li><li>Doubles: 8 + 8 = 16, so 8 + 9 = 17.</li><li>If 9 + 6 = 15, then 15 − 6 = 9 and 15 − 9 = 6.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>8 + 7</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>8 + 2 = 10</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>10 + 5</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 15</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Counting the start</td><td>Count on from the next number.</td></tr><tr><td>The wrong fact</td><td>Start from the total.</td></tr><tr><td>+ or −</td><td>Read the sign.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is the Foundation Phase?",
   "a": "Grade R to Grade 3 in South African schools. Learners are about 7 to 8 years old in Grade 2."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why learn facts by heart?",
   "a": "Then bigger sums are quick."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is a fact family?",
   "a": "3 numbers that make 2 additions and 2 subtractions."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is half of 18?",
   "a": "9."
  }
